# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# PyInstaller
build/
dist/
*.manifest

# Bundled copy of the NaviCore config tool — fetched at build time, never committed.
# The public NaviCore repo is the single source of truth; a committed copy here is a
# fork waiting to happen. See CLAUDE.md "The UI is NOT forked".
src/webui/

# Local user state
*.log
logs/
intellex_config.json
src/webui.prev/

# Bundled copy of the WCB Wizard — same rule as src/webui/ above. The public WCB
# repo is the single source of truth; fetched with tools/fetch_webui.py --tool wcb.
src/webui_wcb/
src/webui_wcb.prev/

# Downloaded copies of the three wikis — fetched with tools/fetch_wiki.py, same
# rule as the tool bundles above. The wikis are their own repos and are the
# single source of truth; a committed copy here is a fork waiting to happen.
src/wiki/
src/wiki.prev/

# Downloaded firmware images, kept so flashing works with no internet (see
# src/fwcache.py). Several MB, refetchable, and each file is already versioned by
# its own name — committing them would just be a slower copy of GitHub.
src/firmware/

# Written by the build scripts; an artefact of one build, never source.
src/build_stamp.py
# Cut from src/assets/intellex-dock-1024.png by scripts/build-macos.command.
# iconutil is macOS-only, so committing it would mean a file only one of the
# two machines can ever regenerate.
src/assets/*.icns

# A redundant archive of "Intellex logo design/", which is committed. Two copies
# of 1.4 MB of PNGs that drift apart the first time the art is touched.
Intellex logo design.zip
